    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0715" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1947v05/pg701"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">880.00/8–1147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-08-11T15:00:00+01:00">August 11, 1947—3
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3203. I had a brief conversation with Bidault on Saturday<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d483-f1"/> along <pb facs="0716" n="702" xml:id="pg702"/> the lines
                    of my telegram No. 2442, June 20.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d483-f2"/> He said he
                    fully appreciates our sympathetic interest and is in agreement that the peoples
                    of Morocco and Tunisia should be approached by the French with constructive,
                    concrete proposals for democratic reforms, and in that connection referred to
                    recent changes in that direction in Morocco and Tunisia. He referred also to the
                    proposed Algerian statute which is now before the National Assembly.</p>
                <p>He added that he would have a “dossier” for me on the subject at an early
                    date.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
